SUMMARY:OSPO Monthly Meetup: Open science for the environment
LOCATION:Gateway Building\, Social Kitchen\, Room 1420
DESCRIPTION:Join us in shaping the future of open source at UC Berkeley\, 
 building on its rich legacy of leadership in open source software developm
 ent. There will be a fireside chat\, a Q&A session\, and community gatheri
 ng time with drinks and snacks! → Attend in person: Register on this pag
 e and join us at 3pm. → Attend online: Sign up here to receive a Zoom li
 nk (https://forms.gle/fKjzxbKFScfAMxks5) and join us at 3:30pm. This month
  we are cohosting with the Eric and Wendy Schmidt Center for Data Science 
 for the Environment. Join us to explore open science in the context of ind
 igenous data sovereignty\, the open infrastructure powering analyses in pa
 rtnership with the National Park Service\, and how the team are integratin
 g LLMs into their platforms. Together\, we can harness the collective inte
 lligence and creativity of the global open source ecosystem to meaningfull
 y transform how knowledge is created and shared.Check out the rest of the 
 series (https://bids.berkeley.edu/programs-initiatives/open-source-program
 -office-ospo)!
URL;VALUE=URI:https://luma.com/7512q9mo
END:VEVENT
